    "mapping_notes": "# tensorrt_llm__llama4Bf16Bf16Gemm__sm_100f\n\n## Reference interface\n\nAll indices below are logical indices. Byte-level layout information from the\nsaved optimized input is retained in interface.json.\n\n| Parameter | Type | Logical shape | Role | Optimized counterpart |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A | bf16 | 1 x 5120 | input | logical activation A |\n| B | bf16 | 128 x 5120 | input | logical weight B; reference rows are output channels |\n| D | bf16 | 1 x 128 | output | D |\n\n## Computation and mapping\n\nThe reference uses A[m,k], B[n,k], and D[m,n]; B is stored with output-channel first.\nD[m,n] = sum_k A[m,k]*B[n,k].\nOptimized A element offset: m*K + k.\nOptimized B element offset: n*K + k.\nOptimized D element offset: m*N + n.\nReferences always store D at m*N+n; compare logical elements after this reindexing.\nThe saved epilogue uses alpha=1 and beta=0; C is not read.\n\n## Validation boundary\n\nCompiled to PTX and numerically checked on CPU. Not compared against an optimized\nGPU execution or proven equivalent. Precision/reduction-order differences follow\nthe mathematical contract in the top-level README.\n\n## Upstream\n\n- https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM/blob/ef567dd9b8919f6ee8b2da1f6f6d0c90206a78f8/cpp/tensorrt_llm/kernels/llama4MinLatencyKernels/llama4Bf16Bf16Gemm.cu\n- https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM/blob/ef567dd9b8919f6ee8b2da1f6f6d0c90206a78f8/cpp/tensorrt_llm/kernels/llama4MinLatencyKernels/llama4Utils.cuh\n"
